{"name":"Teardrop","hex":"#d1eaea","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"teardrop","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["a single tear (clear, salty liquid secreted by the eye).","The shape of a drop of liquid about to fall. (Note that once detached from a surface, a drop changes shape to become spherical)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/teardrop"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tears","blocks":[{"text":"Tears are a transparent fluid secreted primarily by the lacrimal glands found in the eyes of all land mammals. According to the mode of production, tears are classified into four types: basal, closed eye, emotional, and reflex. The basal rate of tear secretion is ~0.5–2.2 μL/min, and irritation can increase secretion by up to ~100-fold, reaching ~300 μL/min. Tears are made up of water, electrolytes, proteins, lipids, and mucins that form layers on the surface of eyes. The four types of tears differ significantly in their composition."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/USMC-04952.jpg/330px-USMC-04952.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tears"},{"title":"Teardrop (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Teardrop\" is a song by English trip hop group Massive Attack. Vocals are performed by Scottish singer Elizabeth Fraser, former lead singer of Cocteau Twins, who also wrote the lyrics. It was released on 27 April 1998 by Circa and Virgin as the second single from the group's third studio album, Mezzanine (1998). A harpsichord-driven track, \"Teardrop\" was originally set to feature vocals from Madonna, whom Massive Attack turned down in favour of Fraser."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/10/Massive_Attack_-_Teardrop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teardrop_(song)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/USMC-04952.jpg/500px-USMC-04952.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/USMC-04952.jpg/1280px-USMC-04952.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/USMC-04952.jpg/500px-USMC-04952.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Human tears","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUSMC-04952.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Crying-girl.jpg/500px-Crying-girl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Crying-girl.jpg/1280px-Crying-girl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Crying-girl.jpg/500px-Crying-girl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A toddler producing tears due to emotional stress or pain","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrying-girl.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Crying_boy.jpg/500px-Crying_boy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Crying_boy.jpg/500px-Crying_boy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Crying boy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrying_boy.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/D._Maria_II_%28BM_1868%2C0612.2285%29.jpg/500px-D._Maria_II_%28BM_1868%2C0612.2285%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/D._Maria_II_%28BM_1868%2C0612.2285%29.jpg/1280px-D._Maria_II_%28BM_1868%2C0612.2285%29